[ti:Week04-Fri.mp3]

[00:00.00]ingredient 熟义 n. 成分，原料；因素，要素 示例 ① At the same time, it has had to contend with angry shareholders, as the rising cost of beef and other ingredients has clobbered its profits. 与此同时，随着牛肉等原材料的成本上涨导致利润一跌再跌，它（汉堡王）不得不去对付那些愤怒的股东。（The Economist） ② Do you know the ingredients of success? 你知道成功的要素吗？
[00:06.92]specific 熟义 a. 明确的，具体的；特定的；特有的， 独特的 示例 ① A prime example Schweitzer and his colleagues cite is the 2004 collapse of energy-trading giant Enron, where managers used financial incentives to motivate salesmen to meet specific revenue goals. 施魏策尔和他的同事引用的一个典型案例就是能源贸易巨头安然公司在 2004年的倒闭。该公司的管理人员曾经用经济奖励来激励其销售人员完成特定的收益目标。（2012. 6）② Our teachers always gave us very specific instructions. 老师们总给我们很明确的指导。
[00:16.54]wretched 熟义 a. 感到不适的；极坏的；悲惨的 示例 ① If democracy works there, why are so many Indian lives still so wretched? 如果印度有民主，为什么如此多的印度人生活仍然悲惨？（The Economist）② Not as wretched as the doomsters claim, but reviving the British economy will take time. 虽然不像末日论者宣称的那样悲惨，但复苏英国经济确实需要一些时间。
[00:23.08]finite 熟义 a. 有限的；限定的 示例 ① What the commodity markets are telling us is that we're living in a finite world, in which the rapid growth of emerging economies is placing pressure on limited supplies of raw materials, pushing up their prices. 商品市场告诉我们的是：我们生活在一个资源有限的世界里， 新兴经济体的迅速发展给有限的原材料供应带来压力，促使原材料价格上涨。（The New York Times）② The global resources are finite. 地球资源是有限的。
[00:31.78]refute 熟义 v. 驳斥；反驳 示例 ① This is obvious in the case of Mr. Powell: Mr. Obama is making liberal use of his endorsement to refute the latest Republican criticism that he is a "socialist". 这在鲍威尔先生这件事情上尤为明显：奥巴马大大方方地利用了鲍威尔对他的支持，对最近共和党指责他是一名“社会主义者”的批评给予了有力的驳斥。（The Economist）② He was able to refute his father's argument. 他能驳倒他父亲的论点。
[00:39.62]shuttle 熟义 n. 来往于两地之间的航班（或班车、火车）；梭子；穿梭‖v. 往返运送；频繁往来 示例 ① Currently, the only vehicles that can take you into space are the space shuttle and the Russian Soyuz, both of which are terribly inefficient. 目前，唯一能送你到太空的交通工具是航天飞机和俄国的 Soyuz太空船，无论哪个效率都非常低。（2006. 12）② We shuttled the customers to the city centre by cars. 我们来来回回地用汽车把顾客运送到市中心。
[00:47.63]specialise 熟义 v. 专门研究（或从事）；专攻 示例 ① In Beijing, Shenwu Thermal Energy Technology Co. specialises in retrofitting China's steel furnaces. 北京神雾热能技术有限公司是一家专门为中国钢铁锅炉做改造的公司。（2007. 12）② He specialises in English. 他专攻英语。
[00:52.83]successor 熟义 n. 接班人，继任人，继承人 示例 ① His successor Cyrus Mistry has several underperforming businesses to deal with as we explained in our cover story at the end of last year. 正如本刊 （《经济学人》）在去年年底封面故事中所阐述的那样，他（拉坦•塔塔）的继任者塞勒斯•密斯特里要去处理一些表现不佳的业务。（The Economist）② I am sure that he is a reliable legitimate successor. 我确信他是个可靠的法定继承人。
[01:00.58]generalise 熟义 v. 归纳，概括；笼统地讲；推想 示例 ① In an age when art was supposed to depict an actual person or event, it came as a shock that this was a painting not of a nightmare, but of the nightmare as a generalised experience. 在一个艺术被认为应该描写真人真事的年代，这幅画的诞生让世人感到震惊，它不是一幅关于噩梦的画，而是对噩梦体验的一次真实再现。（The Economist） ② Please don't generalise a conclusion from a few examples. 请不要从几个事例中归纳出结论。
[01:09.40]proficiency 熟义 n. 熟练，精通 示例 ① Tang-dynasty fashion ranked proficiency at go as one of the "four accomplishments" necessary for a cultivated gentleman, along with lute-playing, calligraphy and painting. 唐朝时盛行把“棋”视为君子必备的“四艺”之一，其他还包括“琴”、“书”、“画”。（The Economist）② Do you acquire proficiency in your major? 你熟练掌握你的专业课了吗？
[01:17.04]persuasion 熟义 n. 劝说，说服 示例 ① The author believes persuasion, rather than punishment, might be the only way to stop people from using mobile phones while driving. 作者认为，劝说而不是惩罚可能是让人们开车时不使用手机的唯一办法。（2009. 12）② Her mother was reached by their persuasion at last. 她的母亲最后终于被他们说服了。
[01:23.55]issue 熟义 n. 议题；问题；争端‖v. 发表；公布； 正式发给 示例 ① Communication was informal; people discussed ideas and issues in the hallways, on a run, or over a beer. 沟通以非正式的方式进行；人们在过道上，在跑步时，甚至是喝酒的时候讨论想法和问题。（2008. 12）② His ability is not at issue; it's his character I'm worried about. 他的能力毫无争议，我担心的是他的人品。
[01:30.33]muscle 熟义 n. 肌肉 示例 ① While you are sitting passively in front of the TV set, your muscles are turning to fat, your complexion is fading, and your eyesight is being ruined. 当你被动地坐在电视机前时，你的肌肉会转变成脂肪，你的肤色会变暗，你的视力也会受损。（2011. 12）② He pulled his muscle in the match. 他在那次比赛中拉伤了肌肉。
[01:36.76]stimulus 熟义 n. 促进因素；刺激物 示例 ① He taunted Germany's Angela Merkel for hesitating over a stimulus plan, declaring that "France is working on it; Germany is thinking about it." 他宣称“法国正在执行经济刺激计划，而德国却还在考虑中”，以此嘲笑德国总理安格拉•默克尔的犹豫不决。（The Economist）② Regard each failure as a stimulus to further efforts. 把每次失利看成对进一步努力的激励。
[01:44.26]texture 熟义 n. 质地；口感；（音乐或文学的）谐和统一感 示例 ① The instinct of your brain registers the word "apple"; it recalls the shape, colour, taste, smell and texture of that fruit. 你的大脑本能地记住了“苹果”这个词， 它能够回忆这种水果的形状、颜色、味道、 气味和口感。（2009. 12）② We could feel the smooth texture of silk. 我们能感觉出丝绸的光滑质地。 语料 Laws are generally found to be nets of such a texture, as the little creep through, the great break through, and the middle-sized are alone entangled in. 法律就是这样一种网：触犯法律的人，小的可以穿网而过，大的可以破网而出，只有中等的才会坠入网中。 （英国诗人申斯通）
[01:56.02]extinct 熟义 a. 灭绝的，绝种的 示例 ① With all that attention paid to them, you'd think these creatures would at least have the gratitude not to go extinct. 它们（海龟）受到了如此多的关注，你可能会认为这些生物至少应该心怀感激而不会走向灭绝了吧。（2009. 6）② Dinosaurs have been extinct for tens of millions of years. 恐龙灭绝已有几千万年了。
[02:02.50]faculty 熟义 n.（大学的）系或院；全体教员 示例 ① Within academic departments, tenure, combined with age-discrimination laws, makes faculty turnover—critical for a university to remain current in changing times—difficult. 在各教学部门内部，终身聘任制以及一些带有年龄歧视色彩的规章制度使得教师流动非常困难，然而教师流动对一所大学在不断变化的时代做到与时俱进至关重要。（2012. 6）② He is the dean of the Faculty of Medicine. 他是医学院院长。
[02:10.90]encounter 熟义 n. 意外的相见；比赛，交锋‖v. 遭遇， 遇到；偶遇 示例 ① But when stress is encountered continually, the body's reactions are more likely to be harmful than helpful to us. 但是当人持续遭遇压力的时候，身体产生的反应更可能对我们有害而非有益。（2008. 12）② I encountered my old friend yesterday. 我昨天偶遇了我的老朋友。
[02:17.10]suspicion 熟义 n. 怀疑，嫌疑；猜疑，疑虑，不放心 示例 ① Japanese history books sometimes disagree with those of its neighbours, and Japan's apologies for its treatment of them during the second world war have not fully allayed their suspicions. 日本历史教科书时而会与邻国教材内容相左，而日本在关于二战期间对待邻国做法方面的道歉也没有完全打消这些国家的疑虑。（The Economist）② I regard his words with suspicion. 我对他的话表示怀疑。
[02:25.47]turbulent 熟义 a. 动荡的；汹涌的；骚动的 示例 ① Inside the government, there is debate as to whether Mr. Obama's arms-length foreign strategy will survive contact with a turbulent world. 政府内部有一个关于奥巴马的“保持距离”外交策略是否可以在动荡的世界中立得住脚的辩论。（The Economist）② My grandpa was born in that turbulent period of history. 我爷爷出生在那个动荡的历史时期。
[02:32.83]stress 熟义 n. 压力；强调；重音‖vt. 强调；重读 示例 ① "When an employee goes on paternity leave and is with his kids, he gets a new kind of training: in how to keep cool under stress," says spokesperson Christine Elberg Holm. 发言人克里斯蒂•埃尔伯格•霍尔姆说：“当一个雇员休陪产假与孩子们待在一起的时候，他实际上获得的是一次新的培训——如何在压力下保持冷静。”（2007. 12）② Stress can be extremely damaging to your health. 压力对你健康的危害极大。
[02:41.23]mechanical 熟义 a. 机械的；呆头呆脑的；擅长于机械原理的 示例 ① But constantly pulling on the front landing gear can lead to mechanical problems. Many pilots would also prefer to be in control of the driving once their aircraft is on the taxiway. 但是经常拉拽飞机的前起落架会导致机械问题。一旦飞机已经落在滑行道上，许多飞行员还是更喜欢自己操纵。（The Economist）② They were using a mechanical shovel to clear up the streets. 他们用机械铲土机清理街道。
[02:49.93]medium 熟义 n. 手段；材料；媒介‖a. 中等的 示例 ① Advertising is following readers out of the door. The rush is almost unseemly, largely because the Internet is a seductive medium that supposedly matches buyers with sellers and proves to advertisers that their money is well spent. 广告跟着读者走了。这个潮流几乎是不合适的，主要是因为网络媒体诱惑力强，据说能将买卖双方撮合在一起，并向广告商证明他们的钱花得值。（The Economist）② The skirt should be washed at medium temperature. 这裙子需用适中温度的水洗。
[02:59.83]chip 熟义 n. 碎片；薄片；缺口；［pl.］炸薯条‖v. 将（土豆等）切条；切下 示例 ① At Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland, Ohio, research scientists have designed a 4-inch silicon chip that holds 700 tiny primitive motors. 在俄亥俄州克利夫兰市的凯斯西储大学，研究科学家们已经设计出一个四英寸硅晶片， 它承载着700个微型简易的发动机。（2011. 12）② It was difficult to find two cups without some kind of chip on them. 很难找到两个没有一点缺口的杯子。
[03:08.31]imperative 熟义 n. 紧要的事；祈使语气‖a. 紧要的；必要的；权威的；祈使的 示例 ① Stern's Mr. Smith points out that the growth imperative required volumes for each product to be big, as they were in mortgage-backed securities and leveraged loans. 斯特恩商学院的史密斯先生指出，增长饥渴症要求每种金融产品都要有巨大的成交量，就像抵押贷款支持证券和杠杆贷款那样。（The Economist）② It's imperative for you to apologise to him immediately. 你必须立即向他道歉。
[03:16.99]tragic 熟义 a. 可悲的；悲惨的；悲剧（风格）的 示例 ① This is tragic because community is so important—perhaps even more important than career. 这真是很可悲，因为社会交往至关重要，甚至可能比职业更重要。（The Economist）② I don't like the tragic atmosphere. 我不喜欢那种悲剧氛围。
[03:22.27]inferior 熟义 n. 下级，属下‖a. 较低的；次等的 示例 ① We are not about to go back to the days when Congress openly worried about inferior races polluting America's bloodstream. 我们不会回到国会公开表示担忧低等民族污染美国血统的时代。（2008. 12）② A cheaper camera is not always inferior to a more expensive one. 便宜的照相机并不总是不如昂贵的好。
[03:28.97]adapt 熟义 vt. 改编；使适应，适应（新情况） 示例 ① Modern urban life in rich countries is not well adapted to large families. 富裕国家的现代都市生活并不适合大家庭。（2010. 12）② Do you think you could adapt to the French culture? 你觉得你能适应法国的文化吗？
[03:33.81]diffuse 熟义 v. 扩散；漫射；传播‖a. 冗长的；弥漫的；松散的 示例 ① America's more diffuse shareholding structure makes such understandings harder to achieve. 更为松散的控股结构决定了美国公司更难就此达成共识。（The Economist）② The light was diffused by the leaves. 树叶使光线漫射。
[03:39.23]complaint 熟义 n. 抱怨，不满；控诉；诉苦 示例 ① However, we do have to challenge the unthinking complaint that the sector does not do enough in taking ideas to market. 但是，对于这种不假思索就说大学在将知识转化为产品方面做得不够的抱怨，我们要提出不同意见。（2011. 12）② I have many complaints about the hotel room. 我对旅馆房间颇为不满。
[03:45.57]disable 熟义 vt. 使丧失能力；使无效 示例 ① Writer friends of mine pay good money to get the Freedom software that enables them to disable the very Internet connections that seemed so emancipating not long ago. 我的一些作家朋友们不惜重金购买“自由”软件来帮助他们禁网，而在不久前能够上网似乎还被看作自由的象征。（2012. 12）② The burglars disabled the alarm to gain entry to the building. 为了进入大楼，窃贼破坏了报警器。
[03:53.66]factor 熟义 n. 因素，要素 示例 ① This is then coupled to a school's picture of what a diverse class should look like, with the result that passport, ethnic origin and sex can all become influencing factors. 于是，这个因素又与学校认为的课堂多样性应该具备的特征相结合，结果还可能受到诸如护照、种族起源、 性别等的影响。（2011. 6）② His persistence is a significant factor in his success. 坚持是他取得成功的重要因素。
[04:01.61]petroleum 熟义 n. 石油，原油 示例 ① Environmentalists feel worried about the petroleum needed to make it. 环保人士为制作它（塑料）所需要的石油担忧。（2011. 12）② The petroleum price will go up next month. 下个月石油价格会上涨。
[04:06.00]switch 熟义 n. (尤其指突然的)改变；开关‖v. 改变， 转变；转换 示例 ① Persuading people to switch their phones off altogether when they get behind the wheel might be the only answer. 劝告人们在开车时关闭手机或许是唯一的办法。（2009. 12）② In nature, animal group often switch from one pattern to another. 在自然界中，动物群体聚集形态往往会从一种转变为另一种。
[04:12.79]competent 熟义 a. 有能力的，能胜任的，称职的 示例 ① A few titles that invest in the kind of investigative stories which often benefit society the most are in a good position to survive, as long as their owners do a competent job of adjusting to changing circumstances. 少数花本钱做那种通常给社会带来最大益处的调查性新闻报道的出版物，只要其所有者能够很好地适应变化的环境，就不用担心生存问题。（The Economist）② He is competent enough to fill that position. 他完全胜任那个职位。
[04:22.02]passive 熟义 n. 被动语态‖a. 被动的，消极的；被动语态的 示例 ① Former senior American officials reported that intellectual property is being stolen on an unprecedented scale, and that passive defenses no longer work. 美国前高官们报告称知识产权盗窃规模空前， 消极防御再也行不通了。（The Economist）② He played a passive role in the game. 他在游戏中扮演了一个被动的角色。
[04:29.19]productive 熟义 a. 生产的；富有成效的；引起的 示例 ① For the small business, there are additional benefits too—staff are more productive, and happier, enabling firms to keep their headcounts and their recruitment costs to a minimum. 对于小型企业而言，（在家办公）还有额外的好处 ——员工工作更有成效，也更加快乐，从而使公司得以将员工人数和招聘成本降到最低。（2009. 12）② Though they work hard, their efforts are not very productive. 他们很努力，但效率不太高。
[04:38.06]suspect 熟义 n. 嫌疑犯‖a. 可疑的；不可信的‖v. 怀疑；推测 示例 ① "We suspect they felt inspired and energised by his victory, so the stereotype threat wouldn't prove a distraction," says Friedman. 弗里德曼说：“我们猜想，他（奥巴马）的胜利鼓舞了他们，使他们产生了力量，因此，这种成见威胁不再对他们构成干扰。”（2010. 6）② He suspected me of telling lies. 他怀疑我说谎。
[04:44.93]orderly 熟义 a. 整齐的，有秩序的；有组织的 示例 ① Mr. Abhisit has said that he has no plan to resign and is not about to crack down on "peaceful and orderly" demonstrations. 艾比希（泰国总理）表示， 他不会辞职，也不会严厉镇压“和平而有秩序的”游行示威。（The Economist）② The crowd was orderly and quiet. 人群很有秩序也很安静。
[04:51.05]objective 熟义 n. 目标，目的；宾语‖a. 客观的；实体的；真实的 示例 ① The core objective for universities which are research-led must be to maximise the impact of their research efforts. 以研究为导向的大学，其核心目标应该是将其研究成果的影响最大化。（2011. 12）② My long-range objective is to be a scientist. 我的长期目标是当一名科学家。
